.\" kpxcd.toml.5 — Man page for the kpxcd configuration file
.TH KPXCD.TOML 5 "2026-05-18" "kpxcd" "File Formats Manual"

.SH NAME
kpxcd.toml \- configuration file for the KeePassXC daemon

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBkpxcd.toml\fR file configures the \fBkpxcd\fR(8) daemon. It is written
in TOML and is read once at daemon startup.

The file defines which KeePass databases to manage, how they should be unlocked,
and the behavior of the Secret Service, SSH agent, and FIDO2 interfaces.

.SH FILE LOCATION
The configuration file is searched in the following order:

.RS
.TP 1.
Command-line: \fBkpxcd \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
.TP 2.
XDG: \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kpxcd/config.toml\fR (if \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is set)
.TP 3.
Default: \fI~/.config/kpxcd/config.toml\fR
.RE

.SH SECTIONS
The configuration file supports the following top-level sections:

.TP
.B [daemon]
Global daemon settings (exactly one).
.TP
.B [[database]]
Database definitions (TOML array of tables; repeat for each database).
.TP
.B [secret_service]
Secret Service D-Bus interface settings.
.TP
.B [ssh_agent]
SSH agent interface settings.
.TP
.B [fido2]
FIDO2 / passkey interface settings.

.SH "[daemon]" SECTION
Controls global daemon behavior.

.TP
.B idle_timeout
Integer. Seconds of inactivity before locking all databases.
.BR 0
(disabled) is the default.
.TP
.B lock_on_screenlock
Boolean. Parsed but not wired yet; screen-lock auto-lock is not implemented.
Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B log_level
String. Minimum log severity: \fB"error"\fR, \fB"warn"\fR, \fB"info"\fR,
or \fB"debug"\fR. Default: \fB"info"\fR.
.TP
.B log_to_journald
Boolean. Log to systemd journal instead of stderr. Useful when running as a
systemd service. Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B ssh_socket_path
String. Path relative to \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR for the SSH agent socket.
Default: \fB"kpxcd/ssh.sock"\fR.
.TP
.B ssh_mode
String. How to handle SSH agent requests:
.RS
.TP
.B "agent"
Act as a full SSH agent (default). Serves keys from the database.
.TP
.B "proxy"
Forward agent requests to the existing \fB$SSH_AUTH_SOCK\fR.
.RE
Default: \fB"agent"\fR.

.SH "[[database]]" SECTION
Defines a KeePass database to manage. Repeat this section for each database.

.TP
.B path
String. \fIRequired.\fR Absolute path to the \fI.kdbx\fR file.
.TP
.B name
String. Human-readable display name. Defaults to the filename without extension.
.TP
.B default
Boolean. Mark this as the default database. At most one database may be default.
Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B auto_unlock
Boolean. Attempt to unlock this database when the daemon starts.
Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B unlock_credential
String. How to obtain the password for auto-unlock. One of:
.RS
.TP
.B "pam"
Unwrap kpxcd's age-sealed credential using a PAM-derived token sent over
\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kpxcd/pam.sock\fR.
.TP
.B "systemd-credential"
Read from a systemd \fBLoadCredential=\fR file descriptor.
.TP
.B "keyfile"
Read a keyfile from disk.
.TP
.B "prompt"
Do not auto-unlock; wait for \fBkpxcctl unlock\fR.
.TP
.B "none"
Database has no password. \fBWarning:\fR trivially openable.
.RE
Default: \fB"prompt"\fR.
.TP
.B systemd_credential_name
String. Name of the systemd credential holding the password. Only used when
\fBunlock_credential = "systemd-credential"\fR. The credential is read from
\fI$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/<name>\fR. Default: empty string.
.TP
.B keyfile
String. Path to a keyfile. Used when \fBunlock_credential = "keyfile"\fR or
as a secondary factor alongside a password. Supports KeePass XML keyfiles
(v1, v2) and raw binary files. Default: empty string.
.TP
.B yubikey_slot
Integer. Reserved for YubiKey challenge-response; current config validation
does not enable \fBunlock_credential = "yubikey"\fR. Default: \fB0\fR.
.TP
.B secret_service_expose_group
String. UUID or name of a group to restrict Secret Service exposure to.
Empty string exposes all groups. Default: empty string.
.TP
.B ssh_auto_add
Boolean. Parsed but not enforced yet; SSH key auto-add currently ignores this
per-database switch. Default: \fBfalse\fR.

.SH "[secret_service]" SECTION
Controls the \fBorg.freedesktop.secrets\fR D-Bus interface. This follows the
GNOME Keyring/libsecret trust model: same-user applications in an unlocked
login session can access exposed secrets unless confirmation is enabled.

.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Expose the Secret Service interface on the session bus.
Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B notify_on_access
Boolean. Show a desktop notification when a secret is retrieved.
Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B notify_cache_ttl
Integer. Seconds to suppress repeat access notifications from the same
app. The first access notifies; further accesses within the window are
silent and refresh the timer. \fB0\fR notifies on every access.
Default: \fB300\fR.
.TP
.B require_confirmation
Boolean. Require Polkit confirmation before returning any secret. When true,
missing caller metadata or unavailable Polkit denies access. Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B confirmation_timeout
Integer. Seconds before the Polkit confirmation dialog times out and is
denied. \fB0\fR means no timeout (user must click). Default: \fB30\fR.

.SH "[ssh_agent]" SECTION
Controls the SSH agent interface.

.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Listen on the SSH agent socket.
Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B remove_on_lock
Boolean. Remove identities from the agent when their database is locked.
Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B confirm_on_use
Boolean. Parsed/stored but not enforced by kpxcd's built-in SSH agent yet.
Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B lifetime
Integer. Parsed/stored but not enforced by kpxcd's built-in SSH agent yet.
Default: \fB0\fR.
.TP
.B security_key_provider
String. Security key provider for \fBsk-ssh-*\fR key types.
\fB"internal"\fR uses the built-in Go SSH implementation.
Default: \fB"internal"\fR.

.SH "[fido2]" SECTION
Reserved FIDO2 / passkey settings. The D-Bus methods currently return not implemented.

.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Reserved; even when set true, current D-Bus methods return not implemented.
Default: \fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B aaguid
String. AAGUID (Authenticator Attestation GUID) reported in attestation
objects. Default: \fB"f8a011f3-8c0a-4d15-8006-17111f9edc7d"\fR
(the KeePassXC software authenticator AAGUID).
.TP
.B algorithms
Array of integers. COSE algorithm IDs supported by the software authenticator:
.RS
.TP
.B \-7
ES256 (ECDSA P-256 with SHA-256)
.TP
.B \-25
ES256K (ECDSA secp256k1 with SHA-256)
.TP
.B \-37
PS256 (RSASSA-PSS with SHA-256)
.TP
.B \-8
EdDSA (Ed25519)
.RE
Default: \fB[\-7, \-8]\fR.
.TP
.B user_verification
String. Reserved user verification preference for future passkey operations. One of:
.RS
.TP
.B "required"
Always require user verification.
.TP
.B "preferred"
Request user verification if available.
.TP
.B "discouraged"
Do not request user verification.
.RE
Default: \fB"preferred"\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Minimal configuration — a single database, no auto-unlock:
.nf
[[database]]
path = "/home/user/Passwords.kdbx"
.fi

.TP
.B Auto-unlock via systemd credential with SSH keys:
.nf
[daemon]
idle_timeout = 900
lock_on_screenlock = false

[[database]]
path = "/home/user/Passwords.kdbx"
name = "Personal"
auto_unlock = true
unlock_credential = "systemd-credential"
systemd_credential_name = "kpxcd-personal"
# Parsed but not enforced yet.
ssh_auto_add = false

[secret_service]
enabled = true
notify_on_access = true
.fi

.TP
.B Full configuration with multiple databases and Polkit confirmation:
.nf
[daemon]
idle_timeout = 900
lock_on_screenlock = false
log_level = "info"
log_to_journald = true
ssh_socket_path = "kpxcd/ssh.sock"
ssh_mode = "agent"

[[database]]
path = "/home/user/Passwords.kdbx"
name = "Personal"
auto_unlock = true
unlock_credential = "systemd-credential"
systemd_credential_name = "kpxcd-personal"
# Parsed but not enforced yet.
ssh_auto_add = false

[secret_service]
enabled = true
notify_on_access = true
notify_cache_ttl = 300
require_confirmation = true
confirmation_timeout = 30

[ssh_agent]
enabled = true
remove_on_lock = true
confirm_on_use = false
lifetime = 0
security_key_provider = "internal"

[fido2]
enabled = false
aaguid = "f8a011f3-8c0a-4d15-8006-17111f9edc7d"
algorithms = [-7, -8]
user_verification = "preferred"
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kpxcd/config.toml
Default configuration file location.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kpxcd (8),
.BR kpxcctl (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
